The study of music and dance is a very effective way to get students interested in the subject. The course will introduce the concepts that can be used to teach or develop an understanding of musical composition, along with the techniques to use for teaching it. This course has been designed for those who have already taken one of the courses in their BSc Music degree programme. It would not be possible without this text if we had only included the following features:
- An introduction to the history of music and its impact on society;
- A brief overview of classical music, including the works by Mozart, Beethoven, Haydn, Chopin, Wagner, Debussy, Puccini, Bach, Schubert, Cézanne, Lise Meitner;
- A comprehensive discussion of key composers of the 19th century;
- Explanations of the main types of music;
- Extensive discussions of all major artists, from Mozart to Elgar.
This book also provides students with an excellent background in studying the history of music, through the development of Western musical styles over time, as well as providing useful examples of how musicians relate to each other and to non-musicians.
– Andrew Leech – Professor of
